-- title:
--   Uniqueness of the Drinfeld transport of a rigidification
-- statement:
--   Fix distinct primes $r$, $\bar r$ and a nonzero level $N$ with $r \nmid N$; a complete discrete valuation ring $\mathcal O$ of characteristic zero with uniformiser $\pi$ whose residue ring has cardinality $r$ and for which $(r) = (\pi)$, with fraction field $K_0$; an $\mathcal O$-algebra $Onr$ which is a domain of characteristic zero, complete for the ideal generated by $\pi$, with that ideal maximal, every element satisfying a monic $\mathcal O$-polynomial modulo $\pi$ and every monic polynomial of positive degree having a root modulo $\pi$, together with an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $Fr$ which is the $r$-power map modulo $\pi$. Let $a, b \in \mathbb Q$ satisfy `IsIndefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt a b r rbar` (so $0 < a$ or $0 < b$, and the completion of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q, a, b]$ at a height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$ is a division algebra exactly when $v$ contains $r$ or $\bar r$), let $\Lambda$ be a maximal order containing the rational integers, and $\mathrm{coord}$ an order coordinate system $\Lambda \to \mathbb{Z}_{p^2} \times \mathbb{Z}_{p^2}$ for $r$. Let $A_0$ be a fake elliptic curve of level $N$ over $Onr/\pi$ carrying, via $\mathrm{coord}$ and formal coordinates $\theta_0$, a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module structure $X_0$ of height $4$; let $\iota : \mathbb{Z}_{p^2} \to Onr$, let $\Phi$ be a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module over $Onr/(r)$ which is special for $\iota$ and of height $4$, let $M$ be a moduli package for $r$ over $Onr$ which is a Zariski sheaf, and let $\eta$ assign to each rigidified object over an $Onr$-algebra with $r$ nilpotent a point of $M$, subject to: on admissible objects over Noetherian bases $\eta$ identifies exactly isomorphic objects, $\eta$ commutes with base change of admissible objects, and every point of $M$ is, after passing to a finite open cover by localisations, $\eta$ of an admissible object. Let $E_0$ be an injective ring homomorphism from the centraliser of the $\mathbb{Z}_{p^2}$-action and of $\varpi$ on $\Phi$ into $M_2(K_0)$ whose image agrees with $M_2(\mathcal O)$ up to a fixed power of $r$, let $\kappa : Onr/\pi \to Onr/(r)$ be compatible with the two quotient maps, and let $\beta_0$ be an isogeny from $\Phi$ to $X_0$ pushed along $\kappa$, of height $4n_0$. Finally let $B$ be a nonzero Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra in which $\pi$ and $r$ are nilpotent and whose only idempotents are $0$ and $1$, let $\psi : Onr \to B$ be an $\mathcal O$-algebra map, and let $x$ be a fake elliptic curve over $B$ together with a rigidification relative to $A_0$ and $\psi$. Suppose $(X, \theta)$ and $(X', \theta')$ both exhibit formal $\mathcal O_D$-module structures on $x$ via $\mathrm{coord}$, and that $j \le 1$, $t$ with $t.X = X$ is a rigidified transport of the data $(\theta_0, \kappa, \beta_0, x, \theta, j)$ and is admissible for the leg $\psi \circ Fr^{-j}$, and likewise $j' \le 1$, $t'$ with $t'.X = X'$ is a transport for $\theta'$, admissible for $\psi \circ Fr^{-j'}$. Then $j = j'$, the integers $t.n$ and $t'.n$ coincide, and $\eta$ assigns to $t$ and to $t'$ the same point of $M$ over the leg $\psi \circ Fr^{-j}$.
--
--   This is the uniqueness half of the Čerednik–Drinfeld transport: a rigidified fake elliptic curve over a connected $\pi$-nilpotent base determines its parity $j$, its rigidification index $n$ and its point in the moduli package independently of the chosen formal coordinates. It is used by the lemmas computing how $n$ changes under Frobenius twists, translations and the Hecke correspondences on the special fibre.
